{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/spanningtrees\/graphprotocols\/graph\/randomspanningtree(using:)"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"randomSpanningTree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"using","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"generator","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"inout","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SG","text":"RandomNumberGenerator","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:13SpanningTrees0A6ForestV","text":"SpanningForest","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/SpanningForest","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"parameters":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The source of randomness."}]}],"name":"generator"}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"return-value","text":"Return Value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The forest’s edges, in the order they joined, and its weight, the number of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edges."}]}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each component is rooted at its first vertex in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" order. Every other vertex, in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that order, starts a random walk that stops on reaching the tree; the walk with its loops"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"erased joins the tree. The result is uniform over the spanning forests that have one tree"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per component, each copy of a parallel edge counting as its own edge. Self-loops are never"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"taken. The forest depends only on the generator’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"next()"},{"type":"text","text":" sequence, so a seeded generator"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reproduces it on every platform."}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(m) plus the walks: the mean hitting time of the root, expected, which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O(n m) at worst and far less on well-connected graphs."}]}],"type":"aside","name":"Complexity","style":"note"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A spanning forest drawn uniformly at random, by Wilson’s algorithm: one uniform spanning"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tree per connected component."}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Method","role":"symbol","title":"randomSpanningTree(using:)","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SpanningTrees\/RandomSpanningTree.swift#L46","fileName":"RandomSpanningTree.swift"},"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P13SpanningTreesE06randomC4Tree5usingAD0C6ForestVyxSiGqd__z_tSGRd__lF","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","modules":[{"name":"SpanningTrees","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{